</figure>


  <p>The problems pile up fast. The matrix is mostly zeros because most word pairs never sit next to each other. Rare words produce tiny, noisy counts. Each row is a 50,000-dimensional vector, which makes similarity calculations expensive. Co-occurrence captures something real about meaning, but it captures it in a form that's computationally awful. It's like keeping your entire life's knowledge as raw CCTV footage. Everything you care about is in there somewhere. It's just not a format you want to work with.</p>

  <!-- VIZ 3: Sparse vs dense -->
